oji:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:13.3px;line-height:normal;-webkit-text-stroke-color:rgb(0,0,0);\"><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-kerning:none;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">&lt;Reading&gt; In class, students will practice intensive reading skills and learn vocabulary by reading articles and completing response tasks for the graded readers.</span></span></span></span></span></p><p class=\"p2\" style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-language-override:normal;font-kerning:auto;font-optical-sizing:auto;font-feature-settings:normal;font-variation-settings:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:13.3px;line-height:normal;-webkit-text-stroke-color:rgb(0,0,0);\"><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-kerning:none;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">&lt; Speaking&gt; EC2 Speaking has four main components: 1) students talk about themselves and their experiences 2) students study practical English items, and 3) students talk freely about a wide range of topics.</span></span></span></span></span></p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-language-override:normal;font-kerning:auto;font-optical-sizing:auto;font-feature-settings:normal;font-variation-settings:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:13.3px;line-height:normal;-webkit-text-stroke-color:rgb(0,0,0);\"><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-kerning:none;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\"><span dir=\"auto\" style=\"vertical-align:inherit;\">&lt;Writing&gt; Students will 1) Practice writing on a given topic for a short period of time 2) Complete a task that involves useful grammar and vocabulary, and 3) Learn basic paragraph structure.</span></span></span></span></span></p>", "授業外学習2": "<p class=\"p1\" style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-language-override:normal;font-kerning:auto;font-optical-sizing:auto;font-feature-settings:normal;font-variation-settings:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:13px;line-height:normal;font-family:\"Helvetica Neue\";\">&lt;Listening&gt;Students will listen to dialogues and story books for homework. They will also study vocabulary.</p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-language-override:normal;font-kerning:auto;font-optical-sizing:auto;font-feature-settings:normal;font-variation-settings:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:13px;line-height:normal;font-family:\"Helvetica Neue\";\">&lt;Reading&gt; Students will read graded readers, write graded reader response tasks, take online quizzes, and study vocabulary.</p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-language-override:normal;font-kerning:auto;font-optical-sizing:auto;font-feature-settings:normal;font-variation-settings:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:13px;line-height:normal;font-family:\"Helvetica Neue\";\">&lt;Writing&gt; Students will complete grammar exercises, write short responses to reading tasks, and develop basic academic paragraphs.</p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-language-override:normal;font-kerning:auto;font-optical-sizing:auto;font-feature-settings:normal;font-variation-settings:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:13px;line-height:normal;font-family:\"Helvetica Neue\";\">&lt;Speaking&gt;&nbsp;</p>"}, "評価": {"教科書/Required texts0": ["You should bring your materials to class on your device (computer/tablet) or print and bring paper copies. If you do not bring a device, you should also bring a dictionary to class. You will also need to buy a pre-paid XReading card for Reading and Listening classes. You must bring headphones to listening classes.&nbsp;"], "学生による授業評価の方法Course Evaluation by Students0": ["Conducted in class"], "学生による授業評価の方法Course Evaluation by Students1": ["Each class subject is arranged on the curriculum based on the Diploma Policy (DP) and Curriculum Policy (CP) established by each faculty and graduate school.By studying this course with DP/CP in mind, you will develop the abilities expected by each faculty and graduate school.The DP, CP, and curriculum table (list of classes, etc.) for each faculty/graduate school are posted in the link below, so please use them as a reference for your study plan.https://kwic.kwansei.ac.jp/cabinet/reference?typeCd=0&amp;cabinetId=557&amp;directLink=1*Link to kwic (only current students can view)"], "成績評価Grading0": ["種別　Type備考　Note", "割合　Percentage", "評価基準等　Grading Criteria etc."], "成績評価Grading1": ["その他／Others (99)", "100 %", "See the Evaluation Note below."], "成績評価Grading2": ["備考　Note ＜Listening＞ Students will be assessed by short listening tests and simple comprehension and vocabulary tests. ＜Reading＞ Students will be assessed through unit tests, book tests, Xreading quizzes, and written responses to graded readers and discussions. ＜Speaking＞ Students will be assessed by speaking tests, homework tests and a Practical English Test. They also have to submit a piece of written homework and participate actively in class. ＜Writing＞Students will be assessed by homework, quizzes, and written assignments."], "更新日時/Date of Update0": ["2026年08月15日 10時30分05秒"], "項番No.0": [], "項番No.1": ["2026年度", "秋学期／Fall", "火曜３時限／Tuesday 3", "秋学期／Fall", "教室未定"], "項番No.2": ["2026年度", "秋学期／Fall", "水曜２時限／Wednesday 2", "秋学期／Fall", "教室未定"], "項番No.3": ["2026年度", "秋学期／Fall", "木曜１時限／Thursday 1", "秋学期／Fall", "教室未定"], "項番No.4": ["2026年度", "秋学期／Fall", "金曜２時限／Friday 2", "秋学期／Fall", "教室未定"]}, "campas": 1, "name": "【100】英語コミュニケーションII　Ｂ／English Communication 2", "管理部署": 7, "単位数": 4, "担当者": "ジョーダン　Ｊ．（JORDAN JENNIFER ALINE） ", "履修基準年度": "１年", "履修登録方法": "予備登録", "緊急授業形態": 0, "開講期": 2, "時限1": 9, "時限1_term": 1, "時限2": 15, "時限2_term": 1, "時限3": 21, "時限3_term": 1, "時限4": 29, "時限4_term": 1, "評価1": 6, "成績評価備考": "備考　Note\n＜Listening＞ Students will be assessed by short listening tests and simple comprehension and vocabulary tests.\n＜Reading＞ Students will be assessed through unit tests, book tests, Xreading quizzes, and written responses to graded readers and discussions.\n＜Speaking＞ Students will be assessed by speaking tests, homework tests and a Practical English Test. They also have to submit a piece of written homework and participate actively in class.\n＜Writing＞Students will be assessed by homework, quizzes, and written assignments."}